  <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">04</span><div class="num">Chapter Four</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="honest">What PLR actually is, said plainly</h2></div>
  <p class="answer reveal">Private label rights means you get a finished product and the legal right to put your name on it, sell it, and keep what you earn. It also means you are not the only person who downloaded the file.</p>
  <p class="reveal">I want to be direct about the second half of that sentence, because the people selling PLR badly tend to leave it out and then their customers feel misled six weeks later.</p>
  <p class="reveal">PLR is not exclusive. Other women will download the same source files you do. If what you want is a product that is unmistakably yours and nobody else's on earth, PLR is the wrong tool and you should build from scratch with my blessing.</p>
  <p class="reveal">But that is a much narrower objection than it first appears — because the source file is not what your customer buys. She buys a finished thing in your colours, under your name, positioned for the specific woman you understand and your competitor doesn't. Two people can start from the same template and end up with products that share nothing a buyer would ever notice.</p>
